finding: Behaviour is not preserved for encoded FieldType descriptors whose decode(0) is nonzero. In src/engine/ecs/storage.ts:get, the old body applied decode to (array[index] ?? 0); HEAD returns 0 before invoking decode when the slot is undefined. Independent reproduction with {ctor:Uint8Array,lanes:1,name:"offset",wgsl:null,encode:x=>x+1,decode:x=>x-1}, initialCapacity=1, get(5): fadf2c48 returns -1; 32476c1e returns 0. FieldType permits this codec. This also affects bound scalar/lane getters. The fixed workload only uses identity-decoded vec4/f32/u32, so its zero-allocation check and the 363 passing tests do not detect this failure of exact behaviour preservation. Allocation measurements otherwise reproduce the stage, and restoring the old set body makes the mixed-set allocation gate fail at 614400 bytes in each 600-frame window.
